{"tool_name":"genomic-signature-fcgr","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"genomic-signature-fcgr","home":"https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/25008-genomic-signature-using-fcgr","summary":"Genomic signature using Chaos game representation of frequencies.","addition_date":"2021-05-05T11:03:27Z","last_update_date":"2021-05-23T11:53:42Z","tool_type":["Library"],"version":["1.0.0.0"],"collections":["File Exchange","MATLAB"],"accessibility":"Open access (with restrictions)","biotools_curie":"biotools:genomic-signature-fcgr","cost":"Free of charge (with restrictions)","credit":[{"name":"Jes\u00fas P. Mena-Chalco","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/profile/1927554-jesus-p-mena-chalco"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"Genomic signature using FCGR","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/oxfordjournals.molbev.a026048","metadata":{"abstract":"We explored DNA structures of genomes by means of a new tool derived from the 'chaotic dynamical systems' theory (the so-called chaos game representation [CGR]), which allows the depiction of frequencies of oligonucleotides in the form of images. Using CGR, we observe that subsequences of a genome exhibit the main characteristics of the whole genome, attesting to the validity of the genomic signature concept. Base concentrations, stretches (runs of complementary bases or purines/pyrimidines), and patches (over- or underexpressed words of various lengths) are the main factors explaining the variability observed among sequences. The distance between images may be considered a measure of phylogenetic proximity. Eukaryotes and prokaryotes can be identified merely on the basis of their DNA structures.","authors":[{"name":"Deschavanne P.J."},{"name":"Fagot G."},{"name":"Fertit B."},{"name":"Giron A."},{"name":"Vilain J."}],"citationCount":213,"date":"1999-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Molecular Biology and Evolution","title":"Genomic signature: Characterization and classification of species assessed by chaos game representation of sequences"},"pmid":"10563018","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Bioinformatics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0091"},{"term":"DNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0654"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"Genomic signature using FCGR","home":"https://bio.tools/genomic-signature-fcgr","version":"1.0.0.0","summary":"Genomic signature using Chaos game representation of frequencies.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:genomic-signature-fcgr:1.0.0.0/lib/www.mathworks.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":120,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"count":1,"year":"2001"},{"count":1,"year":"2002"},{"count":1,"year":"2004"},{"count":1,"year":"2018"},{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":2,"year":"2003"},{"count":2,"year":"2006"},{"count":2,"year":"2016"},{"count":3,"year":"2007"},{"count":3,"year":"2019"},{"count":3,"year":"2026"},{"count":4,"year":"2014"},{"count":4,"year":"2020"},{"count":5,"year":"2011"},{"count":5,"year":"2017"},{"count":6,"year":"2008"},{"count":6,"year":"2024"},{"count":7,"year":"2005"},{"count":7,"year":"2009"},{"count":7,"year":"2012"},{"count":7,"year":"2022"},{"count":7,"year":"2025"},{"count":8,"year":"2010"},{"count":8,"year":"2023"},{"count":9,"year":"2013"},{"count":9,"year":"2015"}],"doi":"10.1093/oxfordjournals.molbev.a026048","pmid":"10563018","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"Genomic signature: characterization and classification of species assessed by chaos game representat